From fc702510314bfd8270adb066218fa6535ca0ea11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:10:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 191/194] glm: per-request experiment policy (tf_policy,
 TF_GLM_POLICY_REQUESTS=1)

One boot can A/B exact kernels request by request. With
TF_GLM_POLICY_REQUESTS=1, rank 0 takes the request body's "tf_policy" mask
(default TF_GLM_POLICY_DEFAULT, else bit 0 from TF_GLM_DFLASH2_COUPLED),
keeps only the bits this boot offers, and sends it in the request's begin
step (Header.a, 0 before). Every rank holds it on the sequence until the
slot's next begin, so it cannot change mid-request. Forwards read it
through Forward.wants / policy.on (glue.Set.policy too). Shared windows
and batched prompts run the bits common to all their sequences, and count
forwards with mixed kernel bits (policy_mixed). The done line ends with
" policy=0x.." only when an engine ran a policy.

Bits (policy.zig, night/swift/POLICY.md): 0 DFlash2 coupled drafts and
5 split-QKVA bypass are wired. 1-4 (small-row router, indexer RoPE
hoist, multi-CTA top-2048, prefill owner rows) are reserved for their
packages.
- Bit 0: coupled mode per lane (Lanes.coupledOf). Coupled sampled
  streams get their own calibration (cal[2], same prior), so a
  single-arm boot behaves as before.
- Bit 5: splitWanted keeps a decode window on the replicated
  [q_a | kv_a], which is loaded beside the slices. The loader's cut
  becomes cuda_weights.qkvaSlice; its logic is unchanged.

Off (no env): the wire carries 0 and every switch and log line is as
before. Tests: test-glm-policy-host (12), test-request-policy-host (2),
GPU tf-cuda-test glm-qkva-split-bits (real K4 layers 3/40/77, TP3/4/6,
rows 1-32: every split output equals the replicated projection's bits).

The per-request policy broadcast follows Codex's analysis
(docs/gpt-sol-new.md, "one immutable request policy"). Split QKVA itself
is knapcio's gr8 PR #84 idea (patch 0149).

